("nine-days-of-navratri-nine-forms-of-durga","Nine Days of Navratri: Day-wise Goddess, Bhog and Puja Guide (Shardiya and Chaitra)","Festivals","Day of Navratri guide: the nine forms of Durga, day-wise bhog, Shardiya Navratri and Chaiti Durga Puja with what to offer each day.",r"day of navratri|shardiya|shardiy|chaiti|chaitra durga",
"Each of the nine nights of Navratri is dedicated to one form of Goddess Durga. Shardiya Navratri falls in Ashwin (Sept–Oct) and Chaitra (Chaiti) Navratri in March–April.",
[("Day-wise forms and bhog",L("<b>Day 1 Shailputri:</b> ghee.","<b>Day 2 Brahmacharini:</b> sugar.","<b>Day 3 Chandraghanta:</b> milk or kheer.","<b>Day 4 Kushmanda:</b> malpua.","<b>Day 5 Skandamata:</b> banana.","<b>Day 6 Katyayani:</b> honey.","<b>Day 7 Kalaratri:</b> jaggery.","<b>Day 8 Mahagauri:</b> coconut.","<b>Day 9 Siddhidatri:</b> sesame.")+"<p>When a tithi is skipped or repeated, the day-count shifts by one. "+N+"</p>"),("Dates","<p>Chaitra Navratri 2026 began 19 March; Sharad (Shardiya) Navratri 2026 began 11 October and ended with Dussehra on 20 October.</p>"),("More","<p>See the full <a href='navratri-dussehra-dates-puja.html'>Navratri and Dussehra dates guide</a>.</p>")],"ganesh-puja"),
("diwali-five-days-calendar","Diwali Days and Calendar: Dhanteras to Bhai Dooj (2025 and 2026)","Festivals","Diwali days 2025 and 2026 calendar: Dhanteras, Naraka Chaturdashi, Lakshmi Puja, Govardhan Puja and Bhai Dooj in order.",r"diwali days|calendar diwali|diwali calendar|diwali 20\d\d calendar",
"Diwali is a five-day festival. Here is the order, with 2025 dates as a worked example.",
[("2025 Diwali calendar",L("<b>Dhanteras:</b> about 18 October.","<b>Naraka Chaturdashi (Choti Diwali):</b> 19–20 October.","<b>Lakshmi Puja:</b> 20–21 October.","<b>Govardhan Puja:</b> about 22 October.","<b>Bhai Dooj:</b> about 23 October.")+f"<p>{N}</p>"),("2026","<p>Dhanteras on 6 November and Lakshmi Puja on 8 November 2026. See <a href='diwali-date-lakshmi-puja-vidhi.html'>the Diwali date and vidhi guide</a>.</p>")],"lakshmi-puja"),
("kawad-yatra-sawan-shivratri","Kawad Yatra and Sawan Shivratri 2025: Jal Date, Time and Rules","Vrat & Tithi","Kawad yatra 2025 jal date and time, Kawad Shivratri 2025 and the rules devotees follow while carrying Ganga jal.",r"kawad|kanwar|kanvar|sawan shivratri",
"Kanwariyas carry Ganga jal from places such as Haridwar to local Shiva temples during Shravan and offer it on Sawan Shivratri.",
[("2025",L("Sawan began on 11 July.","Jalabhishek on Sawan Shivratri: 23 July.")+f"<p>{N}</p>"),("Rules devotees follow",L("Stay barefoot and avoid non-vegetarian food and intoxicants.","Do not place the kanwar on the ground.","Chant Bol Bam and offer jal at the Shivling."))],"rudrabhishek-puja"),
("puja-samagri-list-katha","Puja Samagri List: Basic Items and Katha Samagri (Satyanarayan)","Home Puja","Complete puja samagri list, katha samagri for Satyanarayan and bhoomi poojan samagri, with substitutes if something is missing.",r"samagri|katha|pooja items|puja items",
"A puja needs few things done sincerely. Here is the standard list and the katha extras.",
[("Basic puja samagri",L("Roli, haldi, akshat (rice), moli, supari, paan.","Kalash, coconut, mango leaves.","Diya, ghee, camphor, incense.","Flowers, tulsi, fruits, sweets.","Gangajal and panchamrit (milk, curd, honey, ghee, sugar).")),("Katha samagri (Satyanarayan)",L("Banana leaves or plants for the mandap.","Sheera prasad (suji, ghee, sugar, banana).","Charnamrit, tulsi leaves, yellow cloth.")),("Skip the shopping","<p>Book a pandit with the full samagri kit, see our <a href='satyanarayan-puja.html'>Satyanarayan page</a> and <a href='bhoomi-puja.html'>Bhoomi Puja</a>.</p>")],"satyanarayan-puja"),
("janmashtami-fasting-time","Janmashtami Fast: Timing, Rules and Parana (2025 and 2026)","Vrat & Tithi","Janmashtami fast time, fasting timing 2025 and 2026, what to eat, and when to break the fast.",r"fast|fasting|vrat time|parana",
"Many devotees fast on Janmashtami from sunrise until after the Nishita (midnight) puja, when Krishna is said to be born.",
[("Timing",L("<b>2025:</b> Smarta families observed 15 August and Vaishnavas 16 August.","<b>2026:</b> 4 September.")+"<p>Fast is broken after midnight aarti or next morning at the parana time for your city. "+N+"</p>"),("Types of fast",L("Nirjala (no water).","Phalahar (fruits, milk, sabudana, kuttu).")),("More","<p>See the <a href='janmashtami-2026-date-puja-timing.html'>Janmashtami date and puja guide</a>.</p>")],"satyanarayan-puja"),
("raksha-bandhan-rakhi-festival-date","Raksha Bandhan (Rakhi) Date 2025 and 2026, Muhurat and Bhadra","Festivals","When is the Rakhi festival in 2025 and 2026, Raksha Bandhan shubh muhurat and why Bhadra matters.",r"rakhi|raksha|rakshabandhan",
"Raksha Bandhan is on Shravan Purnima, when sisters tie a rakhi on brothers’ wrists.",
[("Dates",L("<b>2025:</b> 9 August.","<b>2026:</b> 28 August.")+f"<p>{N}</p>"),("Bhadra","<p>Rakhi is traditionally tied outside Bhadra kaal, so the best window is the one after Bhadra ends on that day.</p>")],"lakshmi-puja"),
("pandit-ji-in-noida-greater-noida","Pandit Ji in Noida and Greater Noida for Puja at Home or Society","Home Puja","Book pandit ji in Greater Noida and Noida for Griha Pravesh, Satyanarayan, Rudrabhishek and more at your flat or society.",r"noida|ghaziabad|gurgaon|gurugram|faridabad",
"Apartment living in Noida, Greater Noida and Greater Noida West needs a pandit who can work within society rules and a flat’s space.",
[("Tips for flats",L("Ask your RWA about havan or open flame rules and use a havan kund with a chimney or a smokeless option if needed.","Keep a clean floor space of about 6 by 6 feet.","Share parking details so the pandit can reach on time.")),("What we do","<p>We arrange a pandit for Griha Pravesh, Satyanarayan Katha, Rudrabhishek, Vastu Shanti and sanskar. Fill the booking form and we confirm availability for your sector or society.</p>"),("Book","<p>See <a href='griha-pravesh-puja.html'>Griha Pravesh</a> or <a href='pandit-booking.html'>pandit booking</a>.</p>")],"griha-pravesh-puja"),
